message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "zafra-radar-research: NISAR L-band toolkit for sugarcane harvest detection"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Toledo
    given-names: Juan
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-12
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/OWNER/zafra-radar-research"
keywords:
  - nisar
  - sar
  - l-band
  - sugarcane
  - harvest
  - remote-sensing
  - earth-observation
  - agriculture
abstract: >-
  Per-field sugarcane harvest dates from NISAR L2 GCOV backscatter and L2 GUNW coherence,
  with a cane/non-cane gate, a trained harvest detector, per-date uncertainty and checks
  against VIIRS fires, Sentinel-2 NDVI and MapBiomas. Sites: Morelos (Mexico) and
  Ribeirão Preto (Brazil). NISAR data are provisional; references are optical, not field
  visits.
